WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:05.339
Todd Phillips' Joker movie has finally cast
two of the most recognizable characters in

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:09.070
the DC Comics universe — but the choices
may raise a few eyebrows.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:14.780
Per ComicBook.com, child actor Dante Pereira-Olson
is set to play a young Bruce Wayne, years

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.640
before he steps into the cape and cowl to
become Batman.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.280
In 2015, Pereira-Olsen appeared briefly in
another comic book adaptation, Marvel's Jessica

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.280
Jones.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.290
Acclaimed British actor Douglas Hodge will
take on the role of Alfred Pennyworth, a former

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:33.590
Special Operations Executive operative and
Bruce's loyal butler, and later, legal guardian

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.960
following the deaths of Thomas and Martha
Wayne.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.980
Pereira-Olson's involvement with Joker reunites
him with Joaquin Phoenix, who plays Arthur

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:47.150
Fleck, the failed stand-up comedian who eventually
turns to a life of crime and becomes the Joker.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.440
Pereira-Olson played a younger version of
Phoenix's character in the Lynne Ramsay's

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.760
psychological thriller You Were Never Really
Here.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.739
Pereira-Olson will also act alongside Brett
Cullen, who takes on the role of Thomas Wayne.

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:02.350
Cullen is perhaps best known as Goodwin from
ABC's Lost and briefly appeared in Christopher

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.799
Nolan's Batman trilogy finale The Dark Knight
Rises as a kidnapped Congressman.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:11.030
Traditionally, Batman plays a significant
role in the Joker's transformation into a

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.549
deranged supervillain.

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:16.920
Choosing a child actor to star as Bruce Wayne
opposite an adult who plays the dude who snaps

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.020
and starts terrorizing Gotham City is a bold
choice.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.049
It subverts the idea that the Joker can't
exist without Batman — who committed himself

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.509
to vigilantism following the murders of his
parents — and that Batman can't exist without

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:29.260
the Joker.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:29.820
"No.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:30.640
No.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:31.640
You...

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.860
You, complete me."

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:38.500
Clearly, if Bruce in this universe isn't even
a pre-teen when Joker is old enough to have

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:42.740
a failed career and a few wrinkles on his
face, the Joker doesn't necessarily need a

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.340
billionaire orphan in a batsuit to make him
the criminal he is.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.220
But casting reports indicate that Cullen's
role as Thomas Wayne will be more than just

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.389
flashback fodder.

00:01:51.389 --> 00:01:56.659
So perhaps a later act of the movie will depict
the shooting of the Waynes and place the man-who-will-be-the-Joker

00:01:56.659 --> 00:01:59.259
behind the trigger, just as Batman '89 did.

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:02.700
On the other hand, there's the notion that
Bruce Wayne and the Joker are connected not

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.700
by death but by life — through none other
than Thomas Wayne himself.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.729
Casting reports and industry gossip hint that
the Joker's mother could play a big part in

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:15.549
the film, and one fan theory speculates that
Batman and the Joker will be secret half-siblings.

00:02:15.549 --> 00:02:20.080
Sure, this theory is more than a little out
there, but it does hold some weight.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.459
In the film, Thomas Wayne is reportedly a
far less sympathetic character than he usually

00:02:24.459 --> 00:02:25.459
is.

00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:30.290
Instead of a talented physician and kind philanthropist
who does right by all, he's reportedly a,

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:34.900
quote, "cheesy and tanned businessman who
is more in the mold of a 1980s Donald Trump"

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.969
who runs for mayor of Gotham City.

00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:40.819
Arthur might be so overtaken with anguish
and confusion following the revelation that

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:45.569
Thomas is his father that he grabs a gun and
shoots his biological father and his wife,

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:50.250
Bruce's mother Martha, as a way to gain retribution
for growing up without a father and to make

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.640
young Bruce hurt in the same way he did.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.030
Or it might turn out that Alfred Pennyworth
and the Wayne family won't play that large

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:00.900
a role in the upcoming Joker film, appearing
in limited or even cameo capacities rather

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.360
than as crucial characters.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:07.500
After all, the movie is all about Arthur Fleck
and his eventual change into the Joker, described

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:12.830
as, quote, "an exploration of a man disregarded
by society [that] is not only a gritty character

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.120
study, but also a broader cautionary tale."

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.120
Find out the truth when Joker hits theaters
October 4th, 2019.

